index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..2c167066f35b1324a2f2a3935f4094fcdb4cf84b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/domains/findings/pages/the-wide-badge-variant-union-is-read-by-one-file-and-its-eight-member-subset-by-ten.finding.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+import type { Finding } from "../finding.page-type.ts"
+
+export const theWideBadgeVariantUnionIsReadByOneFileAndItsEightMemberSubsetByTen = {
+  id: "01a07323-840b-7b3f-90da-9a056795a68d",
+  pageTypeSlug: "finding",
+  slug: "the-wide-badge-variant-union-is-read-by-one-file-and-its-eight-member-subset-by-ten",
+  domainSlug: "workspace-package/utils-narrow",
+  claim:
+    "Two exported unions are named `BadgeVariant`, and the eight members of the one in `pages/core/schema/color-rule-variant` are a strict subset of the eighteen in `utils-narrow/badge-variant`. The wide one is read by one file, which draws six of its eighteen; the narrow one is read by ten, all under `pages/`. No file imports both. The eighteen are exactly the eighteen keys of `VARIANT_MAP` in `design/badges/badge`, the table that paints a badge, so the wide union restates the drawing vocabulary and the narrow one holds under half of it. Committed source holds nine declarations spelled `BadgeVariant` rather than two. The module slug `badge-variant` is already held by `utils-narrow`, and a slug is unique among the pages of its page type, so renaming the `color-rule-variant` module to `badge-variant` is refused.",
+  evidence:
+    'Measured 2026-09-05 at HEAD `832fa11720`, read-only. Every count below is a grep over the checkout with `node_modules`, `.git` and `temper/temper-web/dist` left out.\n\nTHE TWO UNIONS, MEMBER BY MEMBER. `utils-narrow/badge-variant/badge-variant.module.code.ts` lines 1-19 declare eighteen: `accent`, `destructive`, `elevation`, `elevation-muted`, `surface`, `normal`, `fine`, `superior`, `epic`, `legendary`, `mythic`, `radiant`, `green`, `blue`, `purple`, `yellow`, `orange`, `red`. `pages/core/schema/color-rule-variant/color-rule-variant.module.code.ts` lines 3-14 derive eight from a `BADGE_VARIANTS` array: `accent`, `elevation-muted`, `green`, `blue`, `purple`, `yellow`, `orange`, `red`. All eight are among the eighteen, so the subset is strict and the ten the wide one adds are `destructive`, `elevation`, `surface` and the seven rarity tiers `normal` through `radiant`.\n\nWHO READS WHICH. Ten files import the `BadgeVariant` symbol from `color-rule-variant`: `pages/core/resolve-badge-variant` and nine components under `pages/ui/components/` (`calendar-time-property-badge`, `date-property-badge`, `instant-property-badge`, `multi-select-popover`, `number-property-badge`, `page-detail-properties-shared`, `progress-property-badge`, `relation-display`, `select-property-badge`). Three further files import that module for `ColorRuleVariant` or `badgeVariantSchema` rather than for `BadgeVariant`, which is why a count of the module\'s importers reads thirteen and a count of the type\'s readers reads ten. Exactly one file imports `@akasha/utils-narrow/badge-variant`: `temper/temper-player-completion/activity-categories/activity-categories.module.code.ts:1`. Its twelve category rows at lines 11-22 spell six distinct values — `orange`, `blue`, `green`, `yellow`, `purple`, `red` — and every one of the six is in the narrow union too, so the twelve members only the wide union carries are reached through that type by nothing. Piping the wide one\'s importer list into a grep for `color-rule-variant` returns nothing, so no file sees both unions.\n\nWHAT THE EIGHTEEN ACTUALLY ARE. `design/badges/badge/badge.module.code.tsx` lines 17-36 hold `VARIANT_MAP` with eighteen keys, in the same order and with the same spellings as the wide union, and line 56 derives a third `BadgeVariant` from it through `VariantProps`. That map is what a `Badge` is drawn from, so the wide union is a hand copy of the drawing table and the narrow union is a hand copy of part of it. Nothing in the tree proves either copy against the map.\n\nNINE DECLARATIONS, NOT TWO. A grep for a line declaring `type BadgeVariant` matches nine files in committed source. Beside the two above and the `cva` alias in `design/badges/badge`, `temper/temper-web/companion-bulk-edit-tag/companion-bulk-edit-tag.module.code.tsx:17-25` declares a local union of eight — `elevation-muted` and the seven rarity tiers — which is a different eight from the narrow one and overlaps it only at `elevation-muted`. `temper/temper-web/effect-badge-types/effect-badge-types.module.code.ts:7` exports `BadgeVariant = "elevation-muted"`, a union of one, read by six temper-web files. Three more are local aliases over a `cva` variant table (`design/badges/badge-toggle-group:9`, `temper/temper-web/bulk-edit-tag:13`, `temper/temper-player-inventory-management-ui/rule-bulk-action-badge:28`) and `temper/temper-progress/activity-categories/properties/badge-variant.text-property.ts:3` is `= string`. Three further copies sit in `temper/temper-web/dist` and are build output, not source.\n\nHOW THIS CAME UP, AND THE SLUG. It surfaced when a rename of the `color-rule-variant` module to `badge-variant` was refused for the slug being taken. `utils-narrow/badge-variant/badge-variant.module.ts:6` states `slug: "badge-variant"` on a `module` page, and `color-rule-variant.module.ts:6` is a `module` page too. `pages/properties/slug.text-property.ts:13` states `unique: "page-type"` and its invariant at line 17 reads "A slug is unique among the pages of its page type", so the two cannot both be `module/badge-variant`. A `text-property` page at `temper/temper-progress/activity-categories/properties/badge-variant.text-property.ts:8` also carries the slug `badge-variant`, which is allowed because it is a different page type.\n\nWHAT I DID NOT ESTABLISH. I did not test the refusal by attempting the rename; the slug collision above is read off the two module pages and the uniqueness rule rather than observed as a refusal message. I did not judge which union is the right one to keep, nor whether the narrow one\'s eight are narrow on purpose — `color-rule-variant.module.ts:7` defines its module as "the named colors a badge is drawn in and a color rule answers", which is consistent with a color-only vocabulary being deliberate. I did not measure whether any value outside the narrow eight ever reaches the components that read it.',
+} as const satisfies Finding
